Z||000000||GTMike||12-16-2001||03:08 PM||||about 18 inches back from the solenoid the line is riped  i cant find the other end  dose any one know where it connects to???<P>thanks||||reg||1
Z||000001||mrfiero||12-16-2001||03:14 PM||||There is a metal vacuum line attached to the firewall......the rubber line connects this metal line to the EGR solenoid.<P>This is the root of most code 32's.....over time the rubber line just falls apart.<P>Get a new rubber line and reattach (it is 7/32").||||reg||1
Z||000002||GTMike||12-16-2001||03:46 PM||||thank you very much  i found it  ||||reg||1
Z||000003||ka4nkf||12-16-2001||10:42 PM||||If you are talking about the line in the back of the solenoid, that is a fresh air line not a vac. line. it goes to the air cleaner.||||reg||1
